    "name_suffix": "_2026",
    "teacher_markdown": "### **Purpose of This Level**\r\n\r\nThis level is designed to help students understand:\r\n\r\n* how **parallel arrays must stay in sync**\r\n* how bugs can occur when only part of a system is updated\r\n* how to **form and test hypotheses** before relying on AI\r\n* how to **evaluate AI explanations**, not just accept them\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Intentional Bugs**\r\n\r\nThere are two built-in bugs:\r\n\r\n1. **Add Stop bug**\r\n\r\n   * `stopNotesArray` is not updated\r\n   * Result: new stops are missing notes or become mismatched\r\n\r\n2. **Remove Stop bug**\r\n\r\n   * `stopHoursArray` is not updated\r\n   * Result: hours no longer match the correct stop\r\n\r\nThese bugs cause the UI to display **desynchronized data**, which students should notice when interacting with the app.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Expected Student Observations**\r\n\r\nStudents should notice:\r\n\r\n* after adding a stop → notes don’t match the correct stop\r\n* after removing a stop → hours shift and no longer align\r\n\r\nStudents should arrive at: All related arrays must be updated together, or the data becomes inconsistent.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n\r\n### **What a Correct Fix Looks Like**\r\n\r\nStudents should add:\r\n\r\n* `stopNotesArray.push(notes)` in `addStop()`\r\n* `stopHoursArray.pop()` in `removeStop()`\r\n\r\nThis ensures all three arrays stay aligned.\r\n\r\n",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "false",
